<title>UK: UK's Watmoughs chief executive resigns.</title>
<headline>UK's Watmoughs chief executive resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British printing group Watmoughs Holdings Plc said on Tuesday that Declan Salter had resigned as chief executive of the group to pursue other interests.</p>
<p>The group said in a statement Patrick Walker, the current chairman and a former chief executive, would be the chief executive.</p>
<p>Walker will, however, be ceo for up to two years while the board seeks a new one.</p>
<p>The company said it would announce interim results on September 17.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
